WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.128
- September 22, three years ago.

00:00:03.128 --> 00:00:06.086
My future is in LA at BuzzFeed.

00:00:06.086 --> 00:00:07.905
I honestly feel my future there.

00:00:07.905 --> 00:00:09.726
That's where I fit
professionally, like my skills

00:00:09.726 --> 00:00:12.105
and interest and personality.

00:00:12.105 --> 00:00:14.585
I am dedicating my time
and thought to being there.

00:00:14.585 --> 00:00:17.502
(melancholy music)

00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:21.945
- I started here at
BuzzFeed very interestingly.

00:00:21.945 --> 00:00:24.276
- Before I was working
here, I was a morning

00:00:24.276 --> 00:00:25.406
show reporter.

00:00:25.406 --> 00:00:27.076
- I actually went to
culinary school and while

00:00:27.076 --> 00:00:31.217
I was in college I made,
like, dumb little, You Tube

00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:34.184
videos and as I started
to kind of play with that,

00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:36.785
I really started to enjoy
the process of editing

00:00:36.785 --> 00:00:37.686
and filming.

00:00:37.686 --> 00:00:39.505
- So I started as a small You Tuber.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.015
I used to make cause play
videos, animated videos,

00:00:42.015 --> 00:00:44.297
and actually two years
ago, I applied to BuzzFeed

00:00:44.297 --> 00:00:45.585
but I didn't get it.

00:00:45.585 --> 00:00:48.025
- I moved to Montana to do
the news which was sort of

00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:50.577
what I thought I wanted to do but I was

00:00:50.577 --> 00:00:52.156
really unhappy there.

00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:54.033
I hated doing the news; I hated the cold;

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.126
I was always alone.

00:00:56.126 --> 00:01:00.756
- I had just lost my job; I
got fired to be more precise.

00:01:00.756 --> 00:01:04.103
- I was at Sephora working
and what I really loved to do

00:01:04.103 --> 00:01:07.966
was helping people find
confidence in themselves

00:01:07.966 --> 00:01:08.886
no matter what.

00:01:08.886 --> 00:01:10.577
So I was doing my little makeup at Sephora

00:01:10.577 --> 00:01:13.345
and then I started seeing a few videos on

00:01:13.345 --> 00:01:16.664
body-positive stuff coming
from this BuzzFeed thing

00:01:16.664 --> 00:01:18.154
and I was like "What the (bleep) is that"?

00:01:18.154 --> 00:01:21.625
- And I remember when I was
still in Montana wishing

00:01:21.625 --> 00:01:24.584
I could move back to LA but
wasn't sure what I wanted

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.743
to do so I eventually
realized I want to make videos

00:01:27.743 --> 00:01:31.385
that make people forget
what their going through.

00:01:31.385 --> 00:01:33.465
- A friend of mine that was
working here gave me the

00:01:33.465 --> 00:01:37.417
suggestion to start writing
just on BuzzFeed.com.

00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:39.225
He was like "You want to work at BuzzFeed?

00:01:39.225 --> 00:01:44.225
They hire people from the
post that, you know, anybody

00:01:44.316 --> 00:01:45.497
posts."

00:01:45.497 --> 00:01:48.297
- There was a point in my
life where it was really

00:01:48.297 --> 00:01:50.006
hard to find a job.

00:01:50.006 --> 00:01:52.156
I would apply to all these
places and for some reason

00:01:52.156 --> 00:01:55.217
I would never get hired
and I wondered if there was

00:01:55.217 --> 00:01:57.716
something wrong with me, like,
if I'm not doing it right.

00:01:57.716 --> 00:02:01.446
- When I looked into it and
I applied for a position

00:02:01.446 --> 00:02:04.246
that I wasn't even qualified for.

00:02:04.246 --> 00:02:06.154
- I was sitting up watching
a lot of late night tv and

00:02:06.154 --> 00:02:09.337
I watched this episode
of the Jimmy Fallon Show

00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:11.025
with Christina Aguilera.

00:02:11.025 --> 00:02:13.063
I was watching and she
did this impersonation of

00:02:13.063 --> 00:02:14.345
Brittany Spears.

00:02:14.345 --> 00:02:17.595
- This little piggy went to the market.

00:02:19.897 --> 00:02:22.097
- So I was quickly, like,
"Oh (bleep), let me write

00:02:22.097 --> 00:02:25.006
this article real quick"
and next thing I know, like,

00:02:25.006 --> 00:02:27.737
it was on the homepage
the next day and it got a

00:02:27.737 --> 00:02:29.345
million views.

00:02:29.345 --> 00:02:31.105
- Two weeks later I got an audition.

00:02:31.105 --> 00:02:34.316
And, my audition, sure
enough, was here for BuzzFeed.

00:02:34.316 --> 00:02:36.785
And I didn't get it but
the person signing me in

00:02:36.785 --> 00:02:40.936
at the desk asked me
my name and he was like

00:02:40.936 --> 00:02:43.305
"Wow there's something
about you; you have a look,

00:02:43.305 --> 00:02:45.055
you have the sounds".

00:02:45.945 --> 00:02:48.865
So, I give him my head shot;
he tells me that I should

00:02:48.865 --> 00:02:51.474
meet someone so right after
my audition he introduces

00:02:51.474 --> 00:02:53.846
me to the team lead for Better Like.

00:02:53.846 --> 00:02:56.305
- I was writing a lot of
these and a lot of my posts

00:02:56.305 --> 00:02:59.977
were getting, like, a million
hits before I was even here.

00:02:59.977 --> 00:03:03.343
- Two years passed and I
remember BuzzFeed again and I

00:03:03.343 --> 00:03:05.623
just had this random thought,
like, oh BuzzFeed, that's

00:03:05.623 --> 00:03:08.834
something I really wanted
to do; might as well try it.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:11.065
- And then within two weeks,
I heard back and they were

00:03:11.065 --> 00:03:13.894
really interested in all the
cooking competitions I had

00:03:13.894 --> 00:03:16.144
done, my professional
experience in restaurants.

00:03:16.144 --> 00:03:18.886
- A few weeks later they
call me in from my head shot

00:03:18.886 --> 00:03:21.017
to film a video.

00:03:21.017 --> 00:03:24.217
(foreign language)

00:03:24.217 --> 00:03:26.825
And, I did an amazing job,
I guess because they called

00:03:26.825 --> 00:03:28.206
me again and they called me
again and then they called

00:03:28.206 --> 00:03:29.276
me again.

00:03:29.276 --> 00:03:32.825
- I was going into an
interview actually that morning

00:03:32.825 --> 00:03:35.505
and I get a phone call from
this number and I answer

00:03:35.505 --> 00:03:38.485
my phone at that point and
now I don't answer any phone

00:03:38.485 --> 00:03:40.977
calls but if its a 310 number,
I'm answering it because

00:03:40.977 --> 00:03:42.476
I don't have a job.

00:03:42.476 --> 00:03:45.736
- Well it turns out they took
me for an interview to be

00:03:45.736 --> 00:03:48.356
a fellow which here that
means you have to have actual

00:03:48.356 --> 00:03:52.939
like, technical skills and
I had zero technical skills.

00:03:54.257 --> 00:03:59.257
So, I came in for an interview
with Eugene of all people.

00:03:59.436 --> 00:04:01.596
I was just like yeah I love
fashion; look at me; I'm

00:04:01.596 --> 00:04:03.337
fashionable; I love fashion.

00:04:03.337 --> 00:04:04.982
And, then they're like "What
about your technical skills".

00:04:04.982 --> 00:04:07.446
And, I was like technically
I love fashion and then

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:08.894
I just moved on.

00:04:08.894 --> 00:04:11.596
- So Dave from HR was on the
other line and he was like

00:04:11.596 --> 00:04:13.646
"Is this Nick Gillery and I
was like yes, this is Nick

00:04:13.646 --> 00:04:16.697
and he was just like so
we saw your community post

00:04:16.697 --> 00:04:19.705
and Macie who runs the
curation team would love to

00:04:19.705 --> 00:04:21.325
have you in for an interview.

00:04:21.325 --> 00:04:22.993
Are you available to
come in this afternoon?"

00:04:22.993 --> 00:04:26.136
I said yes so fast before my
life, I was like absolutely

00:04:26.136 --> 00:04:26.969
yes.

00:04:28.857 --> 00:04:30.217
- And that was that!

00:04:30.217 --> 00:04:33.825
- After I was graduated I
got a call like two or three

00:04:33.825 --> 00:04:36.537
days later and they offered
me the job officially.

00:04:36.537 --> 00:04:39.497
- They gave me a shot and
three months in after that

00:04:39.497 --> 00:04:42.444
they offered me a BuzzFeed producer role.

00:04:42.444 --> 00:04:44.756
- It was really funny coming
across that journal entry

00:04:44.756 --> 00:04:47.897
because that's exactly what
I did; I moved home with the

00:04:47.897 --> 00:04:50.206
intent of working at BuzzFeed;
I interviewed; I didn't

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:53.194
get it and I was devastated.

00:04:53.194 --> 00:04:55.497
But I knew it just a matter
of time and so I applied

00:04:55.497 --> 00:04:57.017
again and I interviewed
again and I got it.

00:04:57.017 --> 00:05:00.606
- The day that I got the phone
call from BuzzFeed telling

00:05:00.606 --> 00:05:04.344
me that I was hired was the
most amazing feeling that

00:05:04.344 --> 00:05:05.566
I have ever had.

00:05:05.566 --> 00:05:08.625
That day, I remember checking
my bank account and I only

00:05:08.625 --> 00:05:11.785
had like six dollars in my
account and it didn't matter

00:05:11.785 --> 00:05:14.046
because I was just so happy.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:17.326
- I didn't book the job that
I initially came to audition

00:05:17.326 --> 00:05:20.726
for; I don't remember what
it even was but I ended up

00:05:20.726 --> 00:05:22.496
where I needed to be.

00:05:22.496 --> 00:05:24.765
- Regardless of whatever road
blocks lie in your way, if

00:05:24.765 --> 00:05:27.886
you feel in your heart that
you belong somewhere, you

00:05:27.886 --> 00:05:30.785
belong doing something
then keep chasing it.

00:05:30.785 --> 00:05:33.625
- You should keep fighting
for, keep doing the things

00:05:33.625 --> 00:05:34.756
you love.

00:05:34.756 --> 00:05:36.766
- Whether you want to be a
doctor, whether you want to

00:05:36.766 --> 00:05:38.116
be a lawyer, an athlete,
anything you want to do, you

00:05:38.116 --> 00:05:38.949
can do.

00:05:40.125 --> 00:05:42.822
You are the God of your
own universe and you can

00:05:42.822 --> 00:05:45.465
create the path that you
want to be on so put you mind

00:05:45.465 --> 00:05:47.246
to it and you can do
whatever you want to do.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:50.686
Trust me because it worked for me.

00:05:50.686 --> 00:05:53.603
(melancholy music)

